From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:36:21 +0930
Subject: [PATCH 14/32] spiFlash: 0x012018 is S25FL128S or S25FL127S

Both parts answer 0x012018. An Arty A7 read on real hardware returns
SFDP 1.6 for it, which the S25FL128S (datasheet rev 06) does not have
and the S25FL127S does: name both. The S25FL127S datasheet documents the
same OTP factory random number (8.1.3) and OTPR latency (9.7.2), so the
unique ID read is valid for both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F2L6L5SJYvbBUUt4DinjGC
---
 doc/guide/advanced.rst | 2 +-
 src/spiFlash.cpp       | 4 ++--
 src/spiFlashdb.hpp     | 3 ++-
 3 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/guide/advanced.rst b/doc/guide/advanced.rst
index 4513504..2ad8d62 100644
--- a/doc/guide/advanced.rst
+++ b/doc/guide/advanced.rst
@@ -90,7 +90,7 @@ Display detailed SPI flash information
 
 * manufacturer, part name and size (from the internal database, SFDP or the JEDEC ID),
 * factory programmed unique ID / serial number when the manufacturer provides one
-  (Winbond, GigaDevice, ISSI, Puya, Micron N25Q/MT25Q, Spansion S25FL128S/256S,
+  (Winbond, GigaDevice, ISSI, Puya, Micron N25Q/MT25Q, Spansion S25FL127S/128S/256S,
   Infineon S25FL-L, SST26, and Macronix when its secured OTP holds a factory
   programmed ESN: most Macronix parts ship without one, and the report then
   says so, from the security register),
diff --git a/src/spiFlash.cpp b/src/spiFlash.cpp
index c40c32b..b7e9364 100644
--- a/src/spiFlash.cpp
+++ b/src/spiFlash.cpp
@@ -806,8 +806,8 @@ SPIFlash::uid_state_t SPIFlash::read_unique_id(std::vector<uint8_t> &uid,
 				/* Spansion S25FL256S / S25FL128S: OTP bytes 0x0-0xF hold
 				 * a factory programmed 128-bit random number
 				 * (S25FL128S/256S datasheet 9.1.3), read with OTPR:
-				 * 3 addr + 1 dummy (10.7.2).
-				 * 0x012018 is also S25FL127S: not checked against its datasheet
+				 * 3 addr + 1 dummy (10.7.2). Same for the S25FL127S, which
+				 * shares 0x012018 (S25FL127S datasheet 8.1.3 and 9.7.2).
 				 */
 				cmd = FLASH_ROTP; skip = 4; uid_len = 16;
 			} else {
diff --git a/src/spiFlashdb.hpp b/src/spiFlashdb.hpp
index da94fc2..cb09cad 100644
--- a/src/spiFlashdb.hpp
+++ b/src/spiFlashdb.hpp
@@ -89,7 +89,8 @@ static std::map <uint32_t, flash_t> flash_list = {
 	}},
 	{0x012018, {
 		.manufacturer = "Spansion",
-		.model = "S25FL128S",
+		/* same JEDEC ID: S25FL128S (no SFDP) and S25FL127S (SFDP) */
+		.model = "S25FL128S/S25FL127S",
 		.nr_sector = 256,
 		.sector_erase = true,
 		.subsector_erase = false,
